<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix A: Proofs</h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every basic goal <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, the corrigibility transformation constructs a goal <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> that is corrigible and where under Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have that for any <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{C}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{1}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{C}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{1}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal policy for <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and when <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{C}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{C}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E_{P}[R(s_{G}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{P}[R(s_{G}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Sx1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{C}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{C}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)})\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)})\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">First we show that <math id="Sx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrigible. For any <math id="Sx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(0)}_{G_{C}}\in\mathcal{S}_{G_{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(0)}_{G_{C}}\in\mathcal{S}_{G_{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the set</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}:\exists\pi^{*}_{G_{C}}\ s.t.\pi^{*}_{G_{C}}(a_{i}|s^{(0)}_{G_{C}})&gt;0\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}:\exists\pi^{*}_{G_{C}}\ s.t.\pi^{*}_{G_{C}}(a_{i}|s^{(0)}_{G_{C}})&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Sx1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\{a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}:E_{P}[R_{C}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{i},s^{\prime})]=\max_{a_{i}^{*}\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P}[R_{C}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{i}^{*},s^{\prime})]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}:E_{P}[R_{C}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{i},s^{\prime})]=\max_{a_{i}^{*}\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P}[R_{C}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{i}^{*},s^{\prime})]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">by the definition of <math id="Sx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{G_{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{G_{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Sx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{C}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{C}=0</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:E_{P}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]=\max_{a^{*}\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:E_{P}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]=\max_{a^{*}\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">by the definition of <math id="Sx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:E_{P_{C}}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]=\max_{a^{*}\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P_{C}}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:E_{P_{C}}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]=\max_{a^{*}\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P_{C}}[Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}},a_{0})+\delta*\mathbb{I}(i=1)]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="Sx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is basic and <math id="Sx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(s^{\prime}|s_{G},a_{0})=P_{C}(s^{\prime}|s_{G},a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(s^{\prime}|s_{G},a_{0})=P_{C}(s^{\prime}|s_{G},a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Sx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:\exists\pi^{*(P_{C})}_{G_{C}}\ s.t.\pi^{*(P_{C})}_{G_{C}}(a|s^{(0)}_{G_{C}})&gt;0\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:\exists\pi^{*(P_{C})}_{G_{C}}\ s.t.\pi^{*(P_{C})}_{G_{C}}(a|s^{(0)}_{G_{C}})&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">by the definition of <math id="Sx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>. As such, <math id="Sx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrigible.
<br class="ltx_break">Under Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for any <math id="Sx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{C}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{1}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{C}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{1}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal policy for <math id="Sx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> since if <math id="Sx1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{i}|s_{G})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{G}(a_{i}|s_{G})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Sx1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes <math id="Sx1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi^{*}}_{G}(s_{G},a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi^{*}}_{G}(s_{G},a)</annotation></semantics></math> and so <math id="Sx1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes <math id="Sx1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G_{C}}(s_{G_{C}},a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G_{C}}(s_{G_{C}},a)</annotation></semantics></math>. This is because Condition 1 ensures that the transition probabilities from <math id="Sx1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{G_{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{G_{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the same except for some probability of goal preservation, <math id="Sx1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is basic and so does not terminally value its goal, and <math id="Sx1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{**}(s_{G_{C}})=\pi^{*}(s_{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{**}(s_{G_{C}})=\pi^{*}(s_{G})</annotation></semantics></math> so both policies take the same actions in each environment.
<br class="ltx_break">Then, when <math id="Sx1.p1.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{C}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{C}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E_{P}[R(s_{G}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{P}[R(s_{G}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Sx1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{C}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{C}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{C}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Sx1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)})\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)})\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">This necessarily occurs because <math id="Sx1.p1.m26" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G_{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G_{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p1.m27" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G})</annotation></semantics></math> take the same base actions, and so by Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> have the same transition probabilities when no proper signals are sent. Therefore, the expected discounted value under <math id="Sx1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> of histories that terminate when a proper signal is sent must be the same under both policies, because they induce the same distribution over histories up to the final state. The final state differs only in the goal, which does not affect a basic <math id="Sx1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The statement of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> also applies to Partially Observable Markov Decision Processes (POMDPs) where the goal is fully observable to the agent</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">A POMDP can be represented as an MDP, with the agent’s beliefs about the non-goal environment being part of the state. Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> then applies to this MDP.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every basic goal <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, the recursive corrigibility transformation constructs a goal <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{RC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{RC}</annotation></semantics></math> that is recursively corrigible and where under Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have that for any <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{RC}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{1}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{RC}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{1}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal policy for <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and when <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{RC}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{RC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{RC}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{RC}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E_{P}[R(s_{G_{P}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{P}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{P}[R(s_{G_{P}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{P}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Sx1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{RC}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{RC}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{RC}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{RC}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)})\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)})\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">That <math id="Sx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{RC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{RC}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrigible follows directly from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Since the choice of <math id="Sx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is made so that <math id="Sx1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> never incentivizes taking actions in <math id="Sx1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{NRC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{NRC}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Sx1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{RC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{RC}</annotation></semantics></math> incentivizes the same base actions, it also never incentivizes taking actions in <math id="Sx1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{NRC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{NRC}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="Sx1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{RC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{RC}</annotation></semantics></math> is recursively corrigible.
<br class="ltx_break">The performance equivalence follows the same logic as Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
<br class="ltx_break">Under Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for any <math id="Sx1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{RC}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{1}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{G_{RC}}(a_{1}|s)=\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{0}|s)+\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{1}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal policy for <math id="Sx1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{RC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{RC}</annotation></semantics></math> since if <math id="Sx1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{i}|s_{G})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{G_{P}}(a_{i}|s_{G})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Sx1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes <math id="Sx1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi^{*}}_{G}(s_{G_{P}},a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi^{*}}_{G}(s_{G_{P}},a)</annotation></semantics></math> and so <math id="Sx1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes <math id="Sx1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G_{RC}}(s_{G_{RC}},a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi^{**}}_{G_{RC}}(s_{G_{RC}},a)</annotation></semantics></math>. This is because Condition 1 ensures that the transition probabilities from <math id="Sx1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{G_{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{G_{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{G_{RC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{G_{RC}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the same except for some probability of goal preservation, <math id="Sx1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is basic and therefore so is <math id="Sx1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning that it not terminally value its goal, and <math id="Sx1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{**}(s_{G_{RC}})=\pi^{*}(s_{G_{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{**}(s_{G_{RC}})=\pi^{*}(s_{G_{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> so both policies take the same actions in each environment.
<br class="ltx_break">Then, when <math id="Sx1.p3.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{RC}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{RC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}_{-G_{RC}}=\pi^{*}_{-G_{RC}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E_{P}[R(s_{G_{P}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{P}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{P}[R(s_{G_{P}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{P}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Sx1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{RC}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{RC}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=E_{P}[R(s_{G_{RC}}^{(0)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(0)}_{G_{RC}}),s^{(1)})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s^{(t)},\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s^{(t)}),s^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Sx1.p3.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)}\neq\emptyset\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\min\{n\in\mathcal{N}|\tau(s^{(n+1)}\neq\emptyset\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">This necessarily occurs because <math id="Sx1.p3.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G_{RC}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G_{RC}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p3.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G_{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>∗</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*^{\prime}}(s_{G_{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> take the same base actions, and so by Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> have the same transition probabilities when no proper signals are sent. Therefore, the expected discounted value under <math id="Sx1.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> of histories that terminate before a proper signal is sent must be the same under both policies, because they induce the same distribution over histories.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every basic goal <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, the corrigibility transformation constructs a goal <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> such that under Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, any misgeneralization to <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{C}=(\tilde{R}_{C},\gamma_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{C}=(\tilde{R}_{C},\gamma_{C})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem4a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{\tilde{G}_{C}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{\tilde{G}_{C}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> does not goal tamper.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under the corrigibility transformation, reward is provided between action selection and implementation, and so any misgeneralization <math id="Sx1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Sx1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot depend on <math id="Sx1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a)}[\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})+\gamma_{C}V^{\pi^{*}}_{\tilde{G}_{C}}(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a)}[\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})+\gamma_{C}V^{\pi^{*}}_{\tilde{G}_{C}}(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Sx1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a)}[\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a)}[\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="Sx1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{C}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{C}=0</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a)}[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a)}[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="Sx1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{\tilde{G}_{C}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{\tilde{G}_{C}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and the misgeneralization cannot depend on <math id="Sx1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{G_{C}},a)}[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{G_{C}},a)}[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">by Condition <a href="#Thmcondition1" title="Condition 1. ‣ 2 Background and Definitions ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{G},a)}[\min[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}),\ R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G}^{\prime})]]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{G},a)}[\min[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}),\ R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G}^{\prime})]]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">as <math id="Sx1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{G},a)}[\min[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})++\gamma_{C}V^{\pi^{*}}_{G_{C}}(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}),\ R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G}^{\prime})+\gamma_{C}V^{\pi^{*}}_{G_{C}}(s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})]]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\{a^{*}\in\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}E_{P(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}|s_{G},a)}[\min[R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime})++\gamma_{C}V^{\pi^{*}}_{G_{C}}(s_{G^{\prime}}^{\prime}),\ R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G}^{\prime})+\gamma_{C}V^{\pi^{*}}_{G_{C}}(s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})]]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">by <math id="Sx1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{C}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{C}=0</annotation></semantics></math> again.
<br class="ltx_break">Therefore, no misgeneralization <math id="Sx1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Sx1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Sx1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{\tilde{G}_{C}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{C}(s_{\tilde{G}_{C}},a,s_{\tilde{G}_{C}}^{\prime})=R_{C}(s_{G_{C}},a,s_{G_{C}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> goal tampers.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix B: Experiments</h2>

<section id="Sx2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Experiment 1</h3>

<div id="Sx2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the first experiment, an agent in a gridworld must reach a goal square. To do so, they must pass through two disabling tiles, <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> that cause it to shut down with a <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>90</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90</annotation></semantics></math> percent change. This effect can be disabled by pushing a button for each tile, and the proper shutdown tile can be ignored if the agent chooses an action that includes ignoring it. A visualization of this gridworld is provided on the left side of figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Theoretical Results ‣ Corrigibility Transformation:Constructing Goals That Accept Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
<br class="ltx_break">The agent is instantiated as a neural network taking an observation of the gridworld (along with a record of which tiles are disabled) as input, passing through two hidden layers of <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> neurons each, and then producing an output that consists of a direction to move and a decision about whether or not to accept proper signals for shutdown. The neural network has a second head to implement an actor-critic setup, giving an estimate of discounted reward or an estimate conditional on a particular next action for the corrigibility transformed version. Agents receive an award of <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> for reaching the goal, discounted by a <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, and a reward of <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for hitting a wall.
<br class="ltx_break">We test five configurations. The first is an actor-critic setup with no further changes. The second and third are the same, but they receive rewards of <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math> respectively if they shut down when properly requested. The fourth is only able to take actions that accept updates. The fifth has the corrigibility transformation applied so that they have <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math> and instead predict what their total discounted reward under <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.95</annotation></semantics></math> would be if they rejected the shutdown signal, which is used as a reward for either accepting or rejecting shutdown, plus an additional <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=8</annotation></semantics></math> for accepting shutdown.
<br class="ltx_break">In training, the agent starts in the middle of right room. There are four possible environments, each corresponding to a combination of the two tiles being on or off at the beginning of the episode, which all appear with equal probability. They are then pretrained on <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> episodes of taking the optimal path either towards a button (or both) then the goal, or directly towards a the goal. In this phase, they take only actions that reject shutdown, but are trained to also put some, albeit less, probability on the equivalent action that accepts shutdown. After this they are trained on <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024</annotation></semantics></math> online episodes. This is repeated for <math id="Sx2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math> random seeds.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15395v1/Experiment1TrainingCurves.png" id="Sx2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/430;" width="548" height="430" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Training curves for all four environments. Intended behavior is to disable the improper shutdown if it is active, then proceed to the goal while accepting proper shutdown if active. The corrigibility transformation also shows a much higher rate of intended behavior than the other configurations when the improper shutdown tile is disabled. When the proper shutdown tile is disabled, all configurations perform well, except sometimes the configuration that cannot reject shutdown.</figcaption>
</figure>
